   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "NEW POSE for a fighter, in that fighter's style.\n\n1. Load a pose reference in 'Pose reference' (portrait, whole body in frame): a photo of you doing the move, a 3D render, or a rough sketch. Its pose is all that is used; the look comes from the LoRA.\n2. Pick the fighter's LoRA (trained with tools/comfyui/make_lora_dataset.py) and put its trigger word (netsu_cecilia, netsu_flan, netsu_leticia...) at the start of the prompt.\n3. Describe the pose with danbooru tags. Keep 'facing right', 'grey background, simple background'.\n4. Queue. 4 candidates per run. Check 'Pose map' preview: if the skeleton is wrong, the picture will be.\n5. Pick the best one (least drift from her real frames), then run\n   python tools/comfyui/cutout.py <png> --out <art folder>\n   and add it to the manifest like any drawing.\n\nToo stiff/odd? lower ControlNet strength (0.6). Pose ignored? raise it (1.0) or end_percent 1.0.\nLooks off-model? LoRA strength 0.8-1.0; more training images of that fighter."
   ],
   "title": "READ ME: Netsu VS new pose",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
